{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "author-images/a-scheme-a-reader-fetches-is-no-reference",
  "title": "A reference in a scheme a reader fetches, opens or runs by itself is refused when its content is built, whatever its case, and so is a compound scheme one of whose parts joined by '+' is such a scheme or a link's; an application's own scheme, mixed-case or compound, and a cloud store the application resolves stay references",
  "notes": "Python's MediaContent._validate_url (roomkit._media_url.is_safe_reference) and roomkit-rs's model::media_url: a reference's scheme, lower-cased and split on +, has no part among the schemes the RFC lists (files on the machine, in an archive or on a share, the network protocols generic readers fetch, the wrappers that read through another protocol, a file or a descriptor, code to run, http and https). A link and a data URI are not read this way. A refused content takes no index: the first accepted event is index 0.",
  "rules": [
    "§6.4"
  ],
